  "narrative": [
    "On 11/06/2026 at approximately 1203 hrs I was dispatched to a reported non-injury rear-end collision at the intersection of Cedar Ave and Summit St. I arrived at 1214 hrs. Both vehicles had been moved to the curb on the east side of Summit St, north of the intersection, and both drivers were present. Neither driver reported any injury.",
    "Statements from both drivers indicate that Unit 1 was stopped northbound on Summit St for a red signal at Cedar Ave and that Unit 2, also northbound, did not stop in time and struck the rear of Unit 1 with its front. Light rain was falling and the roadway was wet.",
    "I observed fresh damage to the rear of Unit 1. The rear bumper cover was pushed in and split near the center, the trunk lid was buckled and would not latch, both tail lamp assemblies were broken and the rear body panel was deformed. I observed fresh damage to the front of Unit 2, including the front bumper cover and grille, with white paint transfer on its bumper cover. Lamp debris from Unit 1 was in the northbound lane.",
    "Both vehicles were driven from the scene. Driver 2 was cited for following too closely. Both drivers exchanged information in my presence and were provided with this report number."
  ],
